    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19748" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gŏmorra</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gŏmorrha</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γόμοῤῥα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the city of Gomorrha</i>, <i>in Palestine</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen.
				10, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">19, 28</span></i> et saep.;
			called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gŏmorrhum</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol.
			40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sol.
			35</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gŏmorrhaeus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Gomorrha</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ruinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 844</span></i>
			.</div>
